# Who gets asked to review what.
#
# There is one maintainer today, so every rule below resolves to the same
# person and none of them change who is requested. They are here because the
# paths they name are the ones where a careless change is expensive, and
# because the moment a second maintainer exists the split should already be
# written down rather than improvised.
#
# Code-owner review is deliberately *not* enforced by the branch ruleset while
# there is one maintainer. GitHub does not let an author approve their own pull
# request, so enforcing it against a sole owner produces a rule that can only
# ever be satisfied by an admin override — which trains everyone to reach for
# the override. Turn it on in the ruleset when a second maintainer arrives.
#
# Last match wins, so the default comes first.

*                           @imohiyoko

# The IR schema is the contract between parsers, enrichers and renderers, and
# it is what a third-party parser is written against. Changing it breaks people
# who are not in this repository. It freezes at v1.0.
/schema/                    @imohiyoko
/docs/schema.md             @imohiyoko

# The conformance corpus *is* the definition of the format. A file added or
# removed here changes what "valid" means.
/schema/testdata/           @imohiyoko

# Supply chain: these decide what runs with a write-scoped token, and what ends
# up inside a binary other people download.
/.github/workflows/         @imohiyoko
/.github/CODEOWNERS         @imohiyoko
/action.yml                 @imohiyoko
/.goreleaser.yaml           @imohiyoko
/go.mod                     @imohiyoko
/go.sum                     @imohiyoko

# Licensing. The binaries embed Graphviz under EPL-2.0; if a dependency changes
# and this file does not, the release is out of compliance.
/LICENSE                    @imohiyoko
/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md     @imohiyoko

# Determinism is enforced by regenerating these and failing on any diff, so a
# change here is either a real behaviour change or a bug.
/examples/three-tier/       @imohiyoko
